  "id": "GHSA-5qf7-2r5p-ppj8",
  "aliases": [],
  "title": "Specially crafted URLs can automatically install and preview an inactive theme from WordPress.org",
  "summary": "If an Administrator opens a specially crafted link and, when prompted, logs in, WordPress can automatically install and preview a theme from WordPress.org without the Administrator having to click the Install button. The theme gets written to disk, it remains inactive, and the Administrator immediately sees its preview. This does not change the live site but it does result in the previewed theme being fully loaded.\r\n\r\nWordPress 7.1.1 has been released containing a fix for the vulnerability, and as a courtesy to users on older branches the fix has been backported to all branches back to 4.8.\r\n\r\nDiscovered and responsibly disclosed by Paulos Yibelo and [pwn.ai](https://pwn.ai/)",
